IP Addressing Plan
The addressing block 172.30.22.0/23 is divided into subnets to support departmental VLANs, printers, and CCTV cameras. Each VLAN is allocated a range that ensures efficient use of addresses while keeping traffic isolated.
•	Courier Operations VLAN: 172.30.22.0/25 → 126 usable addresses for courier staff PCs.
•	Administration VLAN: 172.30.22.128/26 → 62 usable addresses for management PCs.
•	Support VLAN: 172.30.22.192/26 → 62 usable addresses for auxiliary services.
•	Printer VLAN: 172.30.22.256/27 → 30 usable addresses, enough for shared printers.
•	CCTV VLAN: 172.30.22.288/28 → 14 usable addresses, sufficient for four cameras with room for expansion.

Inter VLAN routing will be configured on the Layer 3 switch using SVIs. 
Each VLAN will have a gateway address (first usable IP in the subnet) to manage traffic flow and allow controlled communication where required.
